From 1c852083043acb787731bdb3895c62a67527fe09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Kimathi <kimathi@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:19:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement PDF/Word timetable upload and lecturer allocation
 upload

Timetable upload was completely broken for every format, not just
missing PDF/Word support:
- upload_pipeline.py instantiated TimetableExcelParserService, a class
  that doesn't exist anywhere in the codebase (import was commented
  out) - every upload attempt threw NameError before parsing anything
- Parser output field names (program, room, lecturer, day) didn't
  match what the validator/transformer/persistence layer expects
  (program_code, room_code, lecturer_university_id, day_of_week)
- transformer.py called time.strptime() which doesn't exist on
  datetime.time (only datetime.datetime has it)
- academic_year validation regex only accepted hyphens (2025-2026)
  but the rest of the system uses slashes (2025/2026)
- validate_row required start_time/end_time to already be Python
  time objects, rejecting the string times parsers correctly emit
- persistence.save_rows discarded all per-row error detail behind a
  generic exception whenever every row in a batch failed
- transformer stringified a None lecturer_university_id into the
  literal string 'None' instead of treating it as empty

Fixes, in support of PDF/Word/CSV timetable upload:
- Added file_dispatcher.py to route .xlsx/.xls/.csv/.pdf/.docx to the
  right parser (pdf_timetable_parser.py and docx_timetable_parser.py
  already existed but were never wired in)
- Renamed grid-parser output fields to canonical names; added CSV
  support; extended accepted extensions in constants + validator
- Made TimetableSlot.lecturer nullable - a slot can now be created
  before a lecturer is assigned, since lecturer assignment happens
  via the separate allocation upload
- Made lecturer_university_id optional throughout validation/
  transform/persistence

New: lecturer allocation upload (previously the frontend called
timetable/assign-lecturers/ but the endpoint didn't exist at all -
always 404'd):
- Refactored allocation_parser.py to share row-parsing between a new
  parse_allocation_pdf() and the existing parse_allocation_docx()
- Added AssignLecturersAPIView, wired to /timetable/assign-lecturers/,
  matching lecturer names to unit codes in the current term's
  timetable and updating matching slots
- Tightened an overly-broad header-row heuristic in allocation
  parsing that could misfire on lecturer names containing 'lecturer'

Verified end-to-end against a fresh database: all 4 formats
(xlsx/csv/docx/pdf) parse and persist correctly, no-lecturer uploads
correctly leave the slot unassigned, and allocation upload correctly
matches and fills in the lecturer afterward.
